{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1789666971","published":"2026-09-17T17:43:02Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:09.921718207Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-86145"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-86145","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write in pcre2_dfa_match() because\n     more_workspace() reused a cached recursive-DFA workspace block without\n     checking it was large enough for the request, so a pattern using nested\n     assertions followed by recursion under a small heap limit could overflow\n     the heap allocation (PCRE2 before 10.48)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86145.patch: reject a cached next block smaller\n       than the requested size, and clamp a newly allocated block to the\n       remaining heap allowance without overflowing the size computation, in\n       more_workspace() in src/pcre2_dfa_match.c\n     - CVE-2026-86145","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libpcre2-16-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpcre2-16-0?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.36-2+deb11u1+tuxcare.els2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1789666971.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpcre2-32-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpcre2-32-0?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.36-2+deb11u1+tuxcare.els2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1789666971.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpcre2-8-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpcre2-8-0?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.36-2+deb11u1+tuxcare.els2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1789666971.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpcre2-d